WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.500
Earthrise looks like a sunrise on Earth.

00:02.500 --> 00:05.600
But it was Apollo Eight’s motion
that brought Earth into view.

00:05.600 --> 00:07.400
On their fourth orbit of the Moon,

00:07.400 --> 00:10.700
the crew turned, and Bill Anders
caught the moment on color film.

00:10.700 --> 00:14.950
Decades later, NASA matched the mountains
in the photographs to lunar maps,

00:14.950 --> 00:17.322
tracing the picture back
to the place it was taken.
